        <technology>
            <technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses xml:lang="en">Average processes for producing steel kitchen panels.\n\n# Included processes\nThis data set includes the materials and resources needed for producing steel kitchen front panels per m2. The panel has a mounting plate of corrugated cardboard which is coverd with the steel sheets and pressed. The cardboard core is 2 cm wide and used for front covers. It is assumed that the pressing consumes as much electricity as the steel processing of Franke (kitchen worktop production). Transport is estimated according to the ecoinvent standard distances for Switzerland.; Geography: Data valid for Switzerland</technologyDescriptionAndIncludedProcesses>
